{"book":24,"chapter":35,"context":{"chapter":35,"title":"The Faithful Rechabites","summary":"Jeremiah brings the Rechabite clan into a temple room and sets wine before them, but they refuse: their ancestor Jonadab told them never to drink wine, build houses or farm. Their loyalty to a human father shames Judah's disobedience to God, and God promises the Rechabites a lasting line.","background":"Jonadab son of Rechab had supported Jehu's purge of Baal worship in the northern kingdom more than two centuries earlier (2 Kings 10:15-23). His descendants kept a tent-dwelling life, perhaps as a protest against settled Canaanite culture. They had come into Jerusalem only to escape Nebuchadnezzar's invasion (v. 11) in Jehoiakim's day.","customs":[{"term":"Dwell in tents","verses":"35:7","note":"Living as herders in tents rather than as farmers in houses, the way Israel's ancestors had lived (compare Hebrews 11:9)."}],"watchFor":["The test is set up to be refused (vv. 5–6).","Jonadab's word is kept; God's word, spoken 'rising early,' is ignored (v. 14).","'Shall not want a man to stand before me for ever' (v. 19) echoes 33:17-18."],"connections":["2 Kings 10:15-23","1 Chronicles 2:55","Numbers 6:2-4","Hebrews 11:9"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["הַדָּבָר","hadavar","H1697","HTd/Ncmsa","the word"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher-","H834","HTr","which"],["הָיָה","hayah","H1961","HVqp3ms","it came"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["יִרְמְיָהוּ","yirmeyahu","H3414","HNpm","Jeremiah"],["מֵאֵת","me'et","H854","HR/R","from with"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["בִּימֵי","bimei","H3117","HR/Ncmpc","in [the] days of"],["יְהוֹיָקִים","yehoyakim","H3079","HNpm","Jehoiakim"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["יֹאשִׁיָּהוּ","yoshiyahu","H2977","HNpm","Josiah"],["מֶלֶךְ","melekh","H4428","HNcmsc","[the] king of"],["יְהוּדָה","yehudah","H3063","HNpl","Judah"],["לֵאמֹר","lemor","H559","HR/Vqcc","<to> saying"]],"x":[[12023035,12023035,3],[24001003,24001003,3],[24025001,24025001,3]],"